{"id":"000VFD","title":"Signposts and Signals","author":"jakestilesowen","solvedCount":4,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00","posted":"am 10. Oktober 2026, 15:07 Uhr","rules":"Rules:\n\nNormal 7x7 sudoku rules apply (with irregular regions).\n\nNearly Exhaustive Path:\n\nDraw a path starting in the top left. The path never moves diagonally and never visits a cell twice. 48 out of the 49 cells in the grid must be visited by the path.\n\nSignposts:\n\nThe first cell is a signpost. A signpost with digit N requires the path to travel horizontally to column N or travel vertically to row N. The path then makes a 90 degree turn using its turning cell as the next signpost.\n(e.g. A first digit of 4 could mean travel to row 4, then landing on a 6 would mean to travel to column 6, etc.)\n\nSignals:\n\nThe 5 circles contain five different digits from 1-5. Those digits count how many times the path exits their region.\n\nClick to play on SudokuPad\n\nPlease leave a comment if you enjoy :)","solutionCode":"Row 6","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/bm1oj5qtus","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/bm1oj5qtus","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":7,"cols":7,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00"}